{"tool_name":"auto-drrafter","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"auto-drrafter","home":"https://github.com/auto-DRRAFTER/springer-chapter","license":"Other","summary":"The Rosetta-based \"auto-DRRAFTER\" method builds RNA models into moderate-resolution RNA cryo-EM density as part of the Ribosolve pipeline.","addition_date":"2022-12-20T09:20:48.793380Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:17:14.798335Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Web application","Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:auto-drrafter","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"rhiju@stanford.edu","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"zsu@scu.edu.cn","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.rosettacommons.org/docs/latest/application_documentation/rna/auto-drrafter"},{"type":["Training material"],"url":"https://www.rosettacommons.org/demos/latest/public/auto-drrafter/README"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"cis-regulatory element prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0441"}]}],"name":"auto-DRRAFTER","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-0716-2687-0_13","metadata":{"abstract":"RNA three-dimensional structures provide rich and vital information for understanding their functions. Recent advances in cryogenic electron microscopy (cryo-EM) allow structure determination of RNAs and ribonucleoprotein (RNP) complexes. However, limited global and local resolutions of RNA cryo-EM maps pose great challenges in tracing RNA coordinates. The Rosetta-based \u201cauto-DRRAFTER\u201d method builds RNA models into moderate-resolution RNA cryo-EM density as part of the Ribosolve pipeline. Here, we describe a step-by-step protocol for auto-DRRAFTER using a glycine riboswitch from Fusobacterium nucleatum as an example. Successful implementation of this protocol allows automated RNA modeling into RNA cryo-EM density, accelerating our understanding of RNA structure\u2013function relationships. Input and output files are being made available at https://github.com/auto-DRRAFTER/springer-chapter.","authors":[{"name":"Das R."},{"name":"Kappel K."},{"name":"Luo B."},{"name":"Ma H."},{"name":"Pham P."},{"name":"Rangan R."},{"name":"Su Z."}],"citationCount":6,"date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Methods in Molecular Biology","title":"Auto-DRRAFTER: Automated RNA Modeling Based on Cryo-EM Density"},"pmid":"36227570"}],"topic":[{"term":"Electron microscopy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0611"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"},{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0097"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"auto-DRRAFTER","home":"https://bio.tools/auto-drrafter","license":"Other","summary":"The Rosetta-based \"auto-DRRAFTER\" method builds RNA models into moderate-resolution RNA cryo-EM density as part of the Ribosolve pipeline.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:auto-drrafter/app/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"training_material":true},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":12,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":3,"year":"2023"},{"count":3,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1007/978-1-0716-2687-0_13","pmid":"36227570","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Auto-DRRAFTER: Automated RNA Modeling Based on Cryo-EM Density.","year":2023}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"co